229   c  ABST$Evaluated nuclear structure and decay data for all nuclei with    
229  2c  mass number A=229 ({+229}At, {+229}Rn, {+229}Fr, {+229}Ra, {+229}Ac,   
229  3c  {+229}Th, {+229}Pa, {+229}U, {+229}Np, {+229}Pu, and {+229}Am) are     
229  4c  presented. All available experimental data are compiled and evaluated, 
229  5c  and best values for level and |g-ray energies, quantum numbers,        
229  6c  lifetimes, |g-ray intensities and transition probabilities, as well as 
229  7c  other nuclear properties, are recommended.  Inconsistencies and        
229  8c  discrepancies that exist in the literature are discussed. A number of  
229  9c  computer codes (https://www-nds.iaea.org/public/ensdf_pgm/) developed  
229  Bc  by members of the NSDD network were used during the evaluation         
229  Dc  process.  This work supersedes the earlier evaluation by E. Browne and 
229  Ec  J.K. Tuli (2008Br17), published in {INuclear Data Sheets} {B109}, 2657 
229  xc  (2008).                                                                
229   c  CUT$Literature up to October 23, 2025 was consulted. The main source   
229  2c  used for bibliographic information is the NSR database (2014Pr09):     
229  3c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/.                                                 
229   c  ACKN$The authors express their gratitude to Drs. E. Ricard and C.      
229  2c  Morse from the National Nuclear Data Center (BNL) for their assistance 
