229AT c  2010Al24: {+229}At was produced in a bombardment of a                  
229AT2c  2500 mg/cm{+2}-thick {+9}Be target with a 1 GeV/nucleon {+238}U beam   
229AT2c  at the SIS synchrotron facility at GSI. The fragments were selected    
229AT3c  by the FRagment Separator (FRS) and the isotopic identification was    
229AT4c  made by measuring the magnetic rigidity, velocity, time-of-flight,     
229AT5c  energy loss and atomic number of the ions using two plastic            
229AT6c  scintillators and two multisampling ionization chambers. Production    
229AT7c  cross section was measured and compared with predictions using the     
229AT8c  COFRA and EPAX codes.                                                  
