229RN c  2009Ne03: {+229}Rn was produced in a spallation U(p,X) reaction using  
229RN2c  UC{-x} target and 1.4 GeV pulsed proton beam from the CERN's proton    
229RN3c  Synchrotron Booster accelerator. The measurements were performed at the
229RN4c  double Penning-trap mass spectrometer ISOLTRAP at ISOLDE-CERN facility.
229RN5c  The reaction products diffused from the target into a high-efficiency  
229RN6c  ion source. They were accelerated to 30 keV and separated by a         
229RN7c  high-resolution mass separator. Penning trap mass measurements were    
229RN8c  carried out. Off-line studies were also completed to measure |b decay  
229RN9c  events and the {+229}Rn half life.                                     
229RN c  Other: 2010Al24                                                        
