229RA c  1999Fr33: {+229}Fr activity produced by a spallation of 1-GeV proton   
229RA2c  beam produced from the CERN PS Booster on a UC{-2}-C target coupled to 
229RA3c  a surface ionized Ta(Re) ion source. The resulting ions were separated 
229RA4c  in the online isotope separator and deposited on a moving tape. Two    
229RA5c  independent, but simultaneously operated, measurement stations         
229RA6c  incorporated by a tape transport system were used. The first station   
229RA7c  comprised of NE111A plastic scintillator detector for |b counting,     
229RA8c  BaF{-2} detector for fast-timing gamma-ray measurements, and two HPGe. 
229RA9c  Measured |b-gated singles, |b|g|g(t) and |b|g|g|g coincidences.        
229RAac  singles and |b|g coin, |b|g|g coin, and |b|g|g|g coin. The second      
229RAbc  station consisted of a Si(Li) cooled detector and a MINI-ORANGE filter,
229RAcc  planar and co-axial HPGe detectors and NE102 plastic scintillator      
229RAdc  detector. Measured: conversion coefficients and |b|g-ce(t) coin.       
229RA c  Other (same group): 1992Bo05                                           
229RA cB IB$Deduced by the evaluators from |g-ray transition intensity balances.
229RA2cB There are imbalances at the 107.09-keV and 212.86-keV levels,          
229RA3cB presumably due to the poorly known gamma-ray intensties and            
229RA4cB corresponding mixing ratios for the 26.1-keV and 35.6-keV transitions  
