229TH dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
229TH c  2002Gu15: {+229}Ac source was obtained from the decay chain of         
229TH2c  {+229}Fr, produced by a spallation reaction in a {+232}ThC{-2} target, 
229TH3c  induced by 600 MeV protons from the CERN synchrocyclotron, and         
229TH4c  mass-separated in the on-line isotope separator. The activity was      
229TH5c  deposited on aluminium foils, and after about 40 minutes was           
229TH6c  transported in front of the detectors. In the fast timing measurement  
229TH7c  the francium activity was produced by a spallation reaction in a       
229TH8c  {+238}UC{-2} target, induced by 1 GeV protons from the CERN PS-Booster.
229TH9c  The ions were mass separated in the PSB ISOLDE on-line separator and   
229THac  deposited onto a tape transport system. Detectors: HPGe, LEPS          
229THbc  and BaF{-2} for |g rays, mini-orange electron spectrometer with cooled 
229THcc  Si(Li) for ce. Measured E|g, I|g, Ece, Ice, |b|g|g(t) and |b|g-ce(t)   
229TH c  2006Ru07: {+229}Ac source was obtained from the decay chain of         
229TH2c  {+229}Fr, produced by a spallation reaction in a {+238}UC{-2} target,  
229TH3c  induced by 1 GeV protons from the CERN PS-Booster, mass-separated in   
229TH4c  the on-line isotope separator and deposited on aluminium foil.         
229TH5c  After about 40 min of irradiation and 30 min of cooling time,          
229TH6c  the foil with almost pure activity of {+229}Ac was placed in the center
229TH7c  of the experimental setup. Detectors: HPGe, LEPS and BaF{-2} for |g    
229TH8c  rays, 3-mm-thick plastic scintillator NE111A for |b{-} detection.      
229TH9c  Measured E|g, I|g and |b|g|g(t). Quasi-particle-plus-phonon model      
229THac  calculations                                                           
229TH c  Others: 1973Ch24                                                       
