229TH    229TH IT DECAY                2024EL03,2024TI04,2024ZH4426NDS    202601
229TH  H TYP=FUL$AUT=F.G. KONDEV, J.K. TULI and E. BROWNE$                      
229TH2 H CIT=NDS 208, 397 (2026)$CUT=23-Oct-2025$                               
229TH c  2024El03: {+229m}Th was produced in a vacuum-ultraviolet (VUV) laser   
229TH2c  excitation of three {+229}Th-doped:LiSrAlF{-6} crystals with doping    
229TH3c  concentrations of 5|*10{+16} cm{+-3}, 5|*10{+15} cm{+-3} and 1|*10{+16}
229TH4c  cm{+-3}. The laser delivered 30 pulses per second with a typical       
229TH5c  VUV pulse energy of |J 1|mJ/pulse and a beam diameter of |J 2 mm. The  
229TH6c  crystal under study was held in a vacuum chamber consisting of a       
229TH7c  crystal mount, two VUV-sensitive photomultiplier tubes (PMTs)          
229TH8c  (Hamamatsu R6835/R6836), and a pneumatic shutter system to protect the 
229TH9c  PMTs from direct exposure to the VUV laser. Measured: E|g and |g(t).   
229THac  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
229TH c  2024Ti04: {+229m}Th was produced in a VUV laser excitation of a        
229TH2c  {+229}Th-doped:CaF{-2} crystal with a doping concentration of up to    
229TH3c  5|*10{+18} cm/{+3}. The laser operated at a repetition rate of         
229TH4c  30 Hz, with a pulse duration of 10 ns and mean pulse energy of |?15 |mJ
229TH5c  and beam diameter of |J 3 mm. The crystal was held in a vacuum chamber 
229TH6c  and a spherical mirror was used to collect the crystal fluorescence    
229TH7c  over a large solid angle. The fluorescence is then directed to a Cs-I  
229TH8c  PMT tube by two dielectric mirrors. Measured: E|g and |g(t).           
229TH9c  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
229TH c  2024Zh44: The isomeric state of {+229m}Th was produced in laser        
229TH2c  excitation using a single line of a VUV comb of {+229}Th-doped:CaF{-2} 
229TH3c  crystal with a doping concentration of up to 5|*10{+18} cm/{+3}.       
229TH4c  Low energy photons were measured by performing VUV spectroscopy.       
229TH5c  Measured: E|g, |g(t). Deduced: T{-1/2}, quadrupole moment              
