229PA dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 14-Nov-2024)          
229PA c  2015Ah04: {+229}U was produced via {+229}Th({+4}He,4n) and             
229PA2c  {+230}Th({+3}He,4n) reactions. Milligrams quantities of Th targets     
229PA3c  were bombarded with microamp current of {+4}He and {+3}He beams        
229PA4c  provided by the Argonne 152-cm cyclotron. The uranium activity         
229PA5c  was chemically separated, followed by a mass separation using the      
229PA6c  Argonne electromagnetic isotope separator. Gamma rays were measured    
229PA7c  with a LEPS and a coaxial Ge(Li) detector, while a Si(Li) detector was 
229PA8c  used to detect conversion electrons from the mass-separated sample.    
229PA9c  Measured: E|g, I|g, E(x rays), I(x rays), |g|g coin, |g(Pa x ray) coin,
229PAac  ce, (ce)(Pa X ray) coin. Deduced levels, J|p, |e feedings, log| {Ift}, 
229PAbc  internal conversion coefficients, configurations.                      
229PA c  Others: 1982Ah08, reported a J|p=5/2-, |p5/2[523] level at 0.022 keV   
229PA2c  {I5} above the ground state with T{-1/2}=0.42 |ms {I3}, determined from
229PA3c  a time-difference spectrum between Pa K x rays and 80-400 eV electrons;
229PA4c  1989AhZZ                                                               
229PA c  A J|p=5/2-, |p5/2[523] level was reported in {+229}U |e+|b{++} decay   
229PA2c  by 1982Ah08 at 0.022 {I5} keV above the ground state with              
229PA3c  T{-1/2}=0.42 |ms {I3}, determined from a time-difference spectrum      
229PA4c  between Pa K x rays and 80-400 eV electrons. The subsequent work by    
229PA5c  2015Ah04, did not adopt this level, but the authors pointed out that   
229PA6c  the 241.84-(122.52+119.26) keV closed loop gives a positive difference 
229PA7c  of 0.060 keV {I50}. Thus, the existence of this level cannot           
229PA8c  unambiguously be excluded. Future studies with sub-eV energy           
229PA9c  resolution would be valuable.                                          
