229PU c  2010Kh06: {+229}Pu was produced in |a decay of {+233}Cm following      
229PU2c  {+237}Cf |a decay. The latter was produced in {+204}Pb({+36}S,3n)      
229PU3c  reaction with E({+36}S)=163.6, 170.0, 172.6, 173.0 and 174.3 MeV       
229PU4c  provided by the UNILAC accelerator at GSI. An isotopically enriched    
229PU5c  (>99%) {+204}Pb target was used. Evaporation residues (ERs) were       
229PU6c  separated from the primary beam and target-like ions by the velocity   
229PU7c  filter SHIP and were implanted into a position-sensitive 16-strip Si   
229PU8c  detector (PSSD). A box of six Si detectors surrounded the PSSD to      
229PU9c  detect escape |a and SF events. A Ge clover detector was mounted behind
229PUac  the PSSD for detecting X and |g rays. Measured Er-|a|a(t) correlations 
229PU c  2002CaZU, 2002CaZZ: {+229}Pu was produced in {+198}Pt({+40}Ar,5n)      
229PU2c  reaction with E({+40}Ar)=208 MeV provided by the UNILAC accelerator    
229PU3c  at GSI. An isotopically enriched (95.7%) {+198}Pt target was used.     
229PU4c  Er were separated from the primary beam and target-like ions by        
229PU5c  the velocity filter SHIP and were implanted into a position-sensitive  
229PU6c  Si detector (PSSD). Measured Er-|a|a(t) correlations.                  
229PU c  1994An02: {+229}Pu was produced in {+208}Pb({+26}Mg,5n) reaction with  
229PU2c  E({+26}Mg)=145 MeV provided by the U400 Cyclotron of the FLNR, JINR,   
229PU3c  Dubna. An isotopically enriched (98.7%) {+208}Pb target was used.      
229PU4c  Er were separated from the primary beam and target-like ions by the    
229PU5c  VASSILISSA mass separator and were implanted into a position-sensitive 
229PU6c  Si detector (PSSD). Measured Er-|a|a(t) within 200 ms correlation-time 
229PU7c  window                                                                 
