229PU2c  produced in {+204}Pb({+36}S,3n) reaction. The {+36}S beam with energies
229PU3c  of 163.6, 170.0, 172.6, 173.0 and 174.3 MeV was provided by the        
229PU4c  UNILAC accelerator at GSI. An isotopically enriched (>99% in {+204}Pb) 
229PU5c  target was used. Evaporation residues (ERs) were separated from        
229PU6c  the primary beam and target-like ions by the velocity filter SHIP and  
229PU7c  were implanted into a position-sensitive 16-strip Si detector (PSSD).  
229PU8c  A box of six Si detectors surrounded the PSSD to detect escape |a and  
229PU9c  SF events. A Ge clover detector was mounted behind the Si detector     
229PUac  for detecting X and |g rays. Measured Er-|a|a(t) correlations          
